{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You're here because of new abdominal pain that’s spreading to your back. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started a few days ago. The usual epigastric pain I have suddenly started wrapping around to the right side and back. It’s sharper and different from my normal pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fevers, chills, or vomiting with it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fevers or chills. I’ve been vomiting small amounts, same as usual. But standing up makes me feel like the room is spinning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be from low blood pressure or dehydration. We’ll check your vitals and get some fluids going. You mentioned your J tube—where is it now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It was in my abdominal wall, but the ER team said it wasn’t in the right place and took it out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right. The CT scan confirmed it was malpositioned—ended up in the soft tissue of your abdominal wall, not in the stomach. No infection or fluid collection, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why I’ve been feeling worse? But the pain didn’t go away after removal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The tube wasn’t causing an infection, but its position might have been irritating. The pain continuing suggests something else is going on, or it’s part of your chronic issue flaring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had so many surgeries—gastric bypass, reversal, tubes placed and removed. I just want to know what’s causing this new pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We reviewed your history. The CT and ultrasound didn’t show gallstones, pancreatitis, or obstruction. Your liver enzymes are slightly elevated but not concerning. Lactate was high when you arrived but is improving with fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no clear cause? What about my nutrition? I’ve been struggling to eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a big concern. You’ve been relying on the J tube, which isn’t an option now. Eating by mouth causes pain and vomiting due to gastroparesis. The nutrition team will talk to you about balancing intake without triggering symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood sugar? I’ve been feeling shaky sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re checking your glucose every six hours. You had one reading of 70, which is borderline low. We’re giving you dextrose in your IV fluids to keep it stable. It’s likely from not taking in enough calories."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. What about pain control? Morphine in the ER made me nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching to oral oxycodone, lower dose, as needed. It may help with less nausea. We’ll start low and see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it. I don’t want to depend on narcotics, but I need some relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll aim to use the lowest effective dose and work on a long-term plan with your surgeon. Speaking of, your primary surgeon is at another center, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Dr. Evans at Mercy General. I’ve been followed there for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your complex history, we think it’s best to transfer you there. They know your case well and can discuss options like a gastric pacemaker or other interventions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That would be good. I trust Dr. Evans. But what about now? I still hurt."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-11-28 13:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep managing your pain with oxycodone as needed, continue IV fluids, and monitor your glucose. The nutritionist will come by to go over dietary strategies that might help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-11-28 14:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nutrition team met with you. Any questions from that discussion?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-11-28 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They said small, frequent meals with liquid supplements might help, but I’m scared it’ll make the pain worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-11-28 14:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally valid. We’ll start very slowly, maybe with sips or a few spoonfuls, and see how you do. The goal isn’t to overload but to find a balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-11-28 14:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my vitamin levels? I remember being low before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-11-28 14:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your outpatient labs showed vitamin D deficiency. We’re starting you on 50,000 units once a week. Iron is also low—we’ll discuss IV iron later as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-11-28 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s good to know. I’ve been tired—maybe that’s why."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-11-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today? Any change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-11-29 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but the oxycodone helps a little. I tried a few sips of protein shake—no vomiting yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-11-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. Your blood pressure was a bit low this morning—92/58—but improved with fluids. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-11-29 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been dizzy when I stand. Is that related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-11-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely due to low intake and blood pressure. As we get your nutrition up, that should improve. We’ll keep you on IV fluids until you can take more by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-11-29 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my seizure meds? I took them this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-11-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, levetiracetam is continued twice daily. No changes there. Your last seizure was months ago, so we’re keeping it consistent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-11-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve got your transfer approved to Mercy General. They’ll admit you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-11-30 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Will they consider another feeding tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-11-30 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s risky given your history of misplacement and surgeries. They may discuss IV nutrition or other options, but it’s something to talk through with your surgeon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-11-30 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just don’t want to keep ending up in the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-11-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We all want that. The goal is to get you stabilized and work on a long-term plan. They may also evaluate the gastric pacer for gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-11-30 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that was mentioned before. I’m willing to try anything that might help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day—we’re transferring you to Mercy General. Your condition is stable: pain controlled, vitals normal, no fevers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. What meds am I going with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your home meds continue: levetiracetam, fluoxetine, aripiprazole, metoclopramide, and the others. Plus, oxycodone for breakthrough pain and weekly vitamin D."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I should keep trying small meals?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, slowly. And keep monitoring your blood sugar if you can. The team at Mercy will guide next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I appreciate your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and I hope the next visit is for a follow-up, not another admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team will be here soon. Your husband is on the way to meet you there, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, he’ll be waiting. I feel better knowing I’m going to a team that knows my history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes a big difference. They’ll coordinate with pain management, nutrition, and surgery. We’ll send all your records over."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my wound site? The G-tube area is still draining a bit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s clean, with serosanguinous drainage—normal after removal. Keep it covered, and the team will check it daily. No signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll include wound care instructions in your transfer summary. You’re doing well—just keep up the slow progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and I’ll let the team at Mercy know you’re on your way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2175-12-01 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready for the next step."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2175-11-28 13:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2175-12-01 13:28:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with new-onset right-sided abdominal pain radiating to the back, superimposed on chronic epigastric pain and gastroparesis following multiple bariatric surgeries. Imaging revealed a malpositioned J tube in the anterior abdominal wall, which was removed in the ED. Pain persisted despite narcotic management, and she remained unable to tolerate oral intake, requiring IV fluids and dextrose for hypoglycemia. Nutritional deficiencies, including vitamin D and iron, were addressed. Given the complexity of her case and the need for specialized surgical input, she was transferred to an outside facility where her primary surgeon could coordinate long-term management of pain, nutrition, and possible interventions like a gastric pacemaker. She was discharged in stable condition with a plan to continue home medications, initiate weekly vitamin D, and follow up with her surgical team.",
    "problems": [
      "Displacement of other gastrointestinal prosthetic devices, implants and grafts, initial encounter",
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Unspecified abdominal pain",
      "Vitamin D deficiency, unspecified",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Post Gastric Bypass Hypoglycemia",
      "Chronic nausea and vomiting",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, not intractable, without status epilepticus",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Post-traumatic stress disorder, unspecified",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Other chronic pain"
    ]
  }
}
